		{
			"id": "T-2ky2NT6t5E0ShRp",
			"name": "Pariah Gene (Blank)",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A blank is born, not made: a rare genetic absence that leaves a person's soul all but invisible in the warp, and makes the warp itself recoil from them. Psykers, daemons, and even animals find blanks instinctively unsettling to be near — a \"hole\" where a presence should be. Depicted consistently across Black Library (the Culexus Temple's \"Untouchables,\" Cain-series and Eisenhorn-cycle blanks) and Dark Heresy/Only War's Untouchable career.\n\nDesign: Deliberately carries no Warp or Perils of the Warp modifier: a Pariah's field is the *absence* of the warp, not a channelled act, so none of the framework's activation risk applies. See each child trait for its own derivation. Net for the package: +12 (Null Aura) +10 (Immunity) -3 (Unnerving Void) -10 (Social Stigma) = +9.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Psyker",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tzi2GqL6XH8_-nz9a",
					"name": "Null Aura",
					"local_notes": "Lore: The blank's presence itself smothers nearby psychic workings — the basis for why the Inquisition uses blanks to hunt witches and why daemons fear and hate them.\n\nDesign: Built on Affliction (Basic B35): base 10, the delivered \"Warp- Choked\" disadvantage is valued at -30 points for the enhancement math (+30%), stacked with Area Effect (+50%, B102, 2-yard radius), Always On (-40%, B113, it can't be switched off or aimed), and Emanation (-20%, B111, no ranged attack roll, just proximity).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mIUNwXGaPAziCh01l",
							"name": "Disadvantage Delivered (Warp-Choked",
							"local_notes": "Any Warp-tagged ability used in the area must be rolled again as if failed; already-running continuous Warp effects go inert while inside it.",
							"cost_adj": "+30%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mWrAqiyQsVevR4Icz",
							"name": "Area Effect, 2 yards",
							"cost_adj": "+50%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mLASLvUCNJcnXop1s",
							"name": "Always On",
							"cost_adj": "-40%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mhEYNcbpwsYvfD0FC",
							"name": "Emanation",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 10
				},
				{
					"id": "tUfyETw9jEJKkZD-V",
					"name": "Immunity to Warp-Based Effects",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Warp-based Affliction, Mind Control, Mind Probe, and Fear simply do not work on a Pariah.\n\nDesign: Resistant, Immunity tier (Basic B80: base rarity value x5). Warp- based attacks are treated as an \"occasional\" specific hazard (base 2) for a Pariah, since it is their entire defining trait, giving 2 x 5 = 10.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"base_points": 10
				},
				{
					"id": "tWim4sSYekhNUDvZ5",
					"name": "Unnatural Features (Unnerving Void)",
					"local_notes": "Lore: People and animals find a Pariah's presence quietly, deeply wrong.\n\nDesign: Basic's Unnatural Features (per-level reaction penalty), 3 levels of -1 each.",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Social",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"points_per_level": -1,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 3
				},
				{
					"id": "tuQMbcwUICSkJq-ED",
					"name": "Social Stigma (Feared Blank)",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Feared and, in many sectors, watched or conscripted by the Inquisition and the Officio Assassinorum.\n\nDesign: Basic's Social Stigma (Minority Group), -10 (B155).",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Social",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"base_points": -10
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "TgtzKSsaAuyhxlTtT",
			"name": "Pariah Gene (Untouchable)",
			"local_notes": "Lore: An Untouchable is a blank whose gene runs stronger still — the raw material from which the Officio Assassinorum's Culexus Temple recruits. Their null field is wider, their touch is actively harmful to warp- spawned things, and ordinary people find them nearly impossible to be near for long. This trait models the degree only, not a full Culexus Assassin (animus speculum, etc. belong to that unit's own writeup).\n\nDesign: Same components as Pariah Gene, scaled up: wider Null Aura, a new Soul-Static Discharge that actively harms warp-touched creatures in contact, deeper social cost. Net: +22 (Null Aura) +5 (Soul-Static Discharge) +10 (Immunity) -5 (Unnerving Void) -15 (Social Stigma) = +17.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Psyker",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tFYERcJm87PyoRBo0",
					"name": "Null Aura (Wide)",
					"local_notes": "Lore: See Pariah Gene's Null Aura; the field simply reaches further.\n\nDesign: As Pariah Gene's Null Aura, but Area Effect scaled to the 8-yard tier (+150%, B102) instead of 2 yards.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
