		},
		{
			"id": "tnY4pJ-kP-Epa-5Fc",
			"name": "Vortex of Doom (Great Power)",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Librarius Great Power: a tearing vortex of raw warp-force that can gut a building or a company of tanks, at genuine risk to everything and everyone nearby, caster included. Kept as its own top-level entry (rather than nested inside Librarius) so it can be added, or left out, independently of a Librarian's two ordinary signature powers — it is GM-reference only, in the same \"Beyond play\" bracket the framework reserves for Primarchs and Greater Daemons, not meant for ordinary Librarian play.\n\nDesign: Innate Attack (Crushing, 5/die), 20d starting suggestion, with Explosion at the 16-yard tier (+200%, B106), Armor Divisor (2) (+50%), Preparation Required (-30%, a full turn's channelling), Warp, and Severe Perils. At 20 levels this alone totals in the hundreds of points, deliberately priced in the framework's \"Beyond play\" tier rather than toward ordinary Librarian play.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Psyker",
				"Imperium",
				"Great Power"
			],
			"modifiers": [
